PART A — PaNasMs conditions

1. Combined license and scope

This license consists of Part A and the complete Apache License, Version 2.0,
in Part B. They form one license, not alternative licenses. Every permission
and grant in Part B is subject to Part A; Part A controls any conflict.
For the covered material, references to "this License" in Part B mean this
combined license, including for contributions under Part B, section 5.
The appendix to Part B is a generic example, not a separate license grant.

"Software" means the original PaNasMs code, documentation, build tooling and
other original material expressly offered under this license. Restrictions
also cover copies of that material in modified, renamed or derivative works.
"Licensor" means the relevant rights holder or its authorized representative.
Other capitalized terms have the meanings given in Part B.

Separately identified third-party components and assets retain their own
licenses. This license grants no rights the Licensor does not hold. It does
not apply to independent software merely communicating with PaNasMs through
an API, unless that software contains or is supplied with covered material.
It does not restrict rights available independently under applicable law.

This is a custom source-available license. It is not unmodified Apache 2.0,
standard Commons Clause, or an OSI-approved open-source license. Its sale
restriction structure is inspired by Commons Clause 1.0, but the conditions
in Part A, rather than the standard Commons Clause text, are operative here.

2. Permitted activities

Subject to this combined license, you may use, copy, study, modify and
redistribute the Software. Personal use and use within a business are
permitted without a company-size limit. Free distribution of copies and
forks is permitted subject to sections 3–5 and Part B.

You are not required by this license to publish private modifications or
to distribute source code with object code. Any downstream license for your
own changes must not remove these conditions from the covered material.
You must include this entire combined license with distributed copies.

3. Sales and inclusion in paid products

Without prior written approval and a separate written agreement with the
Licensor authorized to grant the necessary rights, you may not:

(a) Sell, rent, or license copies of the Software for a fee or other
    consideration, including copies within modified or renamed versions.
(b) Incorporate, embed, bundle or otherwise supply the Software as part of
    a product sold, rented or licensed for a fee or other consideration.
    This applies to hardware and software products, NAS appliances,
    storage media, virtual-machine images and container images, including
    products that add substantial independent functionality.
(c) Supply a new or used NAS or other computer for sale or rental with the
    Software installed, preloaded, or included on accompanying media.
(d) Include, require or arrange installation or delivery of the Software
    as part of such a product transaction, even if installation takes
    place after ownership transfers or through a party acting for the seller.

These conditions apply even when the Software is described as free, has no
separate price, or is a small part of the product's total value. Splitting
invoices, changing charge descriptions or nominally transferring hardware
ownership before a bundled installation does not avoid these conditions.
Attribution or an informal acknowledgment is not a commercial agreement.

Selling hardware without the Software is permitted. A purchaser may then
independently obtain and install the Software. A public link to the project
alone is not a prohibited bundle if the transaction includes no copy,
installation or entitlement to installation of the Software.

Section 4 is an express exception for independently purchased services;
those service fees alone do not constitute a prohibited sale under section 3.

4. Paid services on customer-owned equipment

You may charge for installation, configuration, maintenance, repair, training
and technical support on equipment already owned by the customer. You may
make, deliver and install copies and service-related modifications reasonably
necessary for those services, provided all of the following are true:

(a) The customer receives the Software under this combined license and is
    charged for the service, not a software copy, license or access right.
(b) The service is independently purchased for customer-owned equipment,
    not included in, required by, or arranged as part of a paid hardware or
    software product transaction prohibited by section 3.
(c) A service contract or subscription does not make the customer's right
    to continue using copies already received conditional on further fees.
(d) You act on your own behalf, do not imply endorsement by PaNasMs, and
    comply with Part B, section 9, for support or warranty obligations.

Recurring maintenance and support subscriptions are permitted on these
conditions. Service-related copying does not authorize selling a software
product or a device bundle under the description of a service.

5. Attribution and changes

Every distributed copy containing the Software must include a readable notice:

  Based on PaNasMs — Pavlo's NAS Management System, by Pavlo Matviienko
  and contributors. Original project: https://github.com/PaNasMs/panasms

Place this notice in an accompanying NOTICE file, documentation or a normally
accessible legal/about screen. No permanent logo or startup banner is required.
Preserve applicable copyright and third-party notices. Distributed modified
files must carry the change notices required by Part B, section 4(b).
Forks may use a different name but must not imply official status or endorsement.
Attribution does not transfer ownership or confer additional trademark rights.

6. Existing copies and statutory rights

This license applies to material expressly released under it. It does not
revoke rights previously granted for copies obtained under earlier licenses.
Nothing here restricts statutory exceptions or rights that cannot lawfully
be restricted, including any applicable exhaustion or resale rights.

END OF PART A

